{"title":"2017 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(fast_with_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (fast with answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Claire adds the degree measures of the interior angles of a convex polygon and arrives at a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5617f6d8def6056c5921630439d64b56cfa519ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. She then discovers that she forgot to include one angle. What is the degree measure of the forgotten angle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/4602ac77968a2052245a6a2d8209741c16b202d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 37\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 63\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 117\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 143\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 163$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the sum of the interior angles of the polygon is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f221761edb8401bbc37a552144212f5cb670485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lceil\\frac{2017}{180}\\right\\rceil = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"103\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/0414f4f3151ba9c0d1bf976fa139f347e7580474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180\\cdot 12 = 2160$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"118\" height=\"13\" />, so the angle Claire forgot is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a1a471bf7a6105363740687d757aaf47511816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 2160-2017=143\\mod 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"245\" height=\"13\" />. Since the polygon is convex, the angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f3740c0fa809d82273bccfa801d1ab2cb35f7e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e740baa06be8a53ea4c5fc54c12b39a4238eee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)\\ =\\ 143}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"104\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28fast_with_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(fast_with_answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (fast with answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (fast with answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the sum of the interior angles is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, we know that the sum of the angles in a polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db12905b4286e5797e6c76312788e0716c23fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\mod 9$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5617f6d8def6056c5921630439d64b56cfa519ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1becf5ee2724c7cc40de81860da07ace05f214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\mod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, so the answer has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c06a1eb6d971657ffb1e8c450764509a181d2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 \\mod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />. The only answer that is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c06a1eb6d971657ffb1e8c450764509a181d2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 \\mod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f61021f12ab09c5b9c3cfbcd7f6207920ff765b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$143$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n-harsha12345\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4mVtT62THpA\">https://youtu.be/4mVtT62THpA</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A\">2017 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki